  "profileSummary": "Alejandro \"Alex\" Olmedo Rodríguez was a tennis player from Peru with American citizenship. He was listed by the USTA as a \"foreign\" player for 1958, but as a U.S. player for 1959. He helped win the Davis Cup for the United States in 1958 and was the No. 2 ranked amateur in 1959. Olmedo won two Majors in 1959 and the U.S. Pro Championships in 1960, and was inducted into the Tennis Hall of Fame in 1987.",
